# Sensitivity Analysis Design Guide

## Article

**Sensitivity Analysis and Robustness**

## Central claim

Stable conclusions require disturbance. Sensitivity analysis tests which parameters, inputs, assumptions, structures, and scenarios control model outputs. Robustness asks whether conclusions and decisions remain defensible under plausible change.

## Required records

| Record | Purpose |
|---|---|
| parameter_ranges | Documents baseline, low, high, and rationale |
| baseline_output | Preserves the reference model result |
| parameter_sweep | Shows output response across plausible variation |
| sensitivity_summary | Ranks drivers by output range and relative change |
| threshold_fragility | Flags parameters that can cross decision thresholds |
| robustness_assessment_card | Documents model stability, fragility, and use limits |
| structural_sensitivity_note | Preserves model-form uncertainty and alternatives |
